{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771712-war-against-the-pure-2nd-ed-stuff","id":771712,"title":"War Against the Pure 2nd Ed stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T14:14:55-08:00","id":771712,"title":"War Against the Pure 2nd Ed stuff","content":"(Off topic: wooo, two threads in one day, I'm on a role of being helplessly none-creative.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Wayward Sons</b></span><br /> So in preparation for a Werewolf game I have coming up I was reading War Against the Pure, and in particular the\u200b Waywards Son's chapter. And I was thinking pretty much everything in there can be used as is except for Death Rage which uses the 2nd Ed Mechanics, while a Fear &quot;rage&quot; is the same as Death Rage but trying to escape instead of kill. I hit a stump when thinking how to house rule Madness Rage, and I was wondering if anyone had any ideas for houseruling The Madness Rage?<br /> <br /> Also the Parallel Gift (Rated 1-5 dots) Aspect? How would this work? I was thinking of making it a flat 3 Dot Aspect and just letting it work as is. The problem I have is gifts that scale according to renown, I was thinking of tying it to Primal Urge/2 rounded up. Does anyone see any problems with this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Silver Crusade</b><b>\u200b</b></span><br /> Also while on the topic of War Against the Pure, has anyone tackled the Silver Crusade stuff? Once again it looks like most of it works as is. Just the Gift List, which I might just leave it as is and treat like it's an Auspice Gift that any Auspice can access. Unless someone else has a better idea?<br /> <br /> My final question is about War Totems. If an entire pack joins a Crusade do they loose their current totem benefits? Or is it treated as a second totem that they can buy into?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T00:49:43-08:00","id":772148,"title":"","content":"For Gift Facets that scale of Renown just keep the 1-5 dot Aspect progression and use that rating as the relevant Renown. For Facets that don't scale, just consider them a 3 dot Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T05:44:22-08:00","id":772253,"title":"","content":"For scalable gifts, you could treat the gift level purchased as the number of dots of effective renown the shifter has. So Primal Strength (purity 1 level) is a one-dot gift, while Primal strength (purity 5 level) is a 5-dot gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T03:30:59-08:00","id":789661,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the delay guys!<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks for all the help for all the help on the Waywards Son Aspects!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T04:38:28-08:00","id":789673,"title":"","content":"If the Wayward Sons appear in future Werewolf material, I would expect them to receive a fairly significant overhaul in terms of mechanics and background. Renown and Gifts are indeed one particular area where there is now a significant difference and it is just as much thematic as mechanical - what a Gift is has changed from 1e and, in general, Gifts shouldn't be used by supernatural beings other than werewolves with a few very rare exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T11:19:35-08:00","id":789835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771712-war-against-the-pure-2nd-ed-stuff?p=789673#post789673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Wayward Sons appear in future Werewolf material, I would expect them to receive a fairly significant overhaul in terms of mechanics and background. Renown and Gifts are indeed one particular area where there is now a significant difference and it is just as much thematic as mechanical - what a Gift is has changed from 1e and, in general, Gifts shouldn't be used by supernatural beings other than werewolves with a few very rare exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd be very much interest in such a supplement. Wayward Sons I thought was much better done, and a much more interesting idea than Changing Breeds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Has for Gifts and Renown. I had actually forgotten that the Wayward Son's used Renown, so I may just drop it altogether to keep book keeping down, and let Wayward Son's use a nerfed Parallel Aspect that doesn't use Renown in it's activation roll to keep Werewolves the masters of Gifts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do thing at least that the Wayward Son's fall into one of those &quot;rare exceptions&quot;, considering that Wayward Son's treat Silver the exact same way Forsaken do. (Even the Minotaurs have a weakness to Silver despite their association with Helios) So there is some connection to Luna there, at least in first edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T12:17:15-08:00","id":789859,"title":"","content":"I think fluffwise any use of facets would need to be &quot;This is not actually the facet, we're just using the mechanics of one to save brain power.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:39:03-08:00","id":789928,"title":"","content":"Facets or Facet-like mechanics would still need traits to base how powerful they turn out to be, ie. Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T16:02:06-08:00","id":789967,"title":"","content":"Yeah considering the changes I'd see the Wayward Sons losing their vulnerability to silver in favor of something else. A lot has changed in second edition and that seems like a minor one. Outside of the cat and birds, they don't really follow the hunter angle so it's easier to imagine them as some sort of thing.<br /> <br /> But, and I've said this before, if we do get a gallery of Pangaeans, I sincerely hope they're not limited to were-animals, considering the vast variety of potential concepts you have in Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T06:17:14-08:00","id":790233,"title":"","content":"I think both Dave B and Acrozatarim mentioned a Mountain Pangaean, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T06:21:31-08:00","id":790234,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but whenever people start talking about wanting shapeshifters they usually only mention animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}